.* WRKJOBSCDE: the job schedule's entries, laid out as the V7R1M0
.* capture (golden/verified/oracle71/panels).
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NBRCL BASETYPE='CHAR 6'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 4'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=DATECL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=FRQCL BASETYPE='CHAR 9'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=RCYCL BASETYPE='CHAR 7'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 30'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=JOB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=STATUS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=SDATE CLASS=DATECL.
:VAR NAME=STIME CLASS=DATECL.
:VAR NAME=FRQ CLASS=FRQCL.
:VAR NAME=RCYACN CLASS=RCYCL.
:VAR NAME=NXTDATE CLASS=DATECL.
:VAR NAME=TEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=ENTRY CLASS=NBRCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=ENTRIES VARS='OPT JOB STATUS SDATE STIME FRQ RCYACN NXTDATE TEXT ENTRY'.
:KEYL NAME=SCDKEYS HELP='KEYS/SCDKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F6 ACTION='CMD ?ADDJOBSCDE'.F6=Add
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display job queue data
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKJOBSCDE KEYL=SCDKEYS HELP=WRKJOBSCDE ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=DATETIME.Work with Job Schedule Entries
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATAC.
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=ENTRIES.(No job schedule entries to display)
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGJOBSCDE JOB(&JOB.) ENTRYNBR(&ENTRY.)' HELP='WRKJOBSCDE/OPTIONS'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDJOBSCDE JOB(&JOB.) ENTRYNBR(&ENTRY.)' HELP='WRKJOBSCDE/OPTIONS'.3=Hold
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD RMVJOBSCDE JOB(&JOB.) ENTRYNBR(&ENTRY.)' HELP='WRKJOBSCDE/OPTIONS'.4=Remove
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD WRKJOBSCDE JOB(&JOB.) OUTPUT(*PRINT)' HELP='WRKJOBSCDE/OPTIONS'.5=Display details
:LISTACT OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSJOBSCDE JOB(&JOB.) ENTRYNBR(&ENTRY.)' HELP='WRKJOBSCDE/OPTIONS'.6=Release
:LISTACT OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKSBMJOB' HELP='WRKJOBSCDE/OPTIONS'.8=Work with last submission
:LISTACT OPTION=10 ENTER='CMD SBMJOB CMD(CALL QCMD) JOB(&JOB.)' HELP='WRKJOBSCDE/OPTIONS'.10=Submit immediately
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKJOBSCDE/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=JOB USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/JOB'.Job
:LISTCOL VAR=STATUS USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/STATUS'.Status
:LISTGRP COL=SCHED.-----Schedule------
:LISTCOL VAR=SDATE USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=27 HELP='FLD/SDATE'.Date
:LISTCOL VAR=STIME USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=38 HELP='FLD/STIME'.Time
:ELISTGRP.
:LISTCOL VAR=FRQ USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=48 HELP='FLD/FRQ'.Frequency
:LISTCOL VAR=RCYACN USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=59 HELP='FLD/RCYACN'.Recovery Action
:LISTCOL VAR=NXTDATE USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=69 HELP='FLD/NXTDATE'.Next Submit Date
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT JOB STATUS SCHED FRQ RCYACN NXTDATE'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKJOBSCDE.Work with Job Schedule Entries - Help
:P.The jobs the schedule submits, with when each runs next and how
often. F6 adds an entry.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/SCDKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F6=Add
:PD.Runs ADDJOBSCDE.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F11=Display job queue data
:PD.Display job queue data.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJOBSCDE/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOB'.Job
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STATUS'.Status
:P.The status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SDATE'.-----Schedule------ date
:P.The -----Schedule------ date of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STIME'.-----Schedule------ time
:P.The -----Schedule------ time of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FRQ'.Frequency
:P.The frequency of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RCYACN'.Recovery Action
:P.The recovery Action of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/NXTDATE'.Next Submit Date
:P.The next Submit Date of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKJOBSCDE/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change Job
Schedule Entry (CHGJOBSCDE) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Job
Schedule Entry (HLDJOBSCDE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it. The Remove Job
Schedule Entry (RMVJOBSCDE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display details
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display details it. The
Work with Job Schedule Entries (WRKJOBSCDE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Job Schedule Entry (RLSJOBSCDE) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Work with last submission
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with last submission
it. The Work with Submitted Jobs (WRKSBMJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.10=Submit immediately
:PD.Type 10 next to an entry and press Enter to submit immediately it.
The Submit Job (SBMJOB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
